There are two contradicting assertions about this I found in the 
spoilers.  The praying spoiler at 

http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/pray.html

states

| Attempting to convert an altar by sacrificing at a non-coaligned 
| altar can convert *you* instead if your alignment is negative

and 

| (If your alignment is positive, the altar will be converted 
| smoothly with probability (YourLevel+2)/(YourLevel+8)

However, the spoiler at 

http://www.helsinki.fi/~vviitane/spoilers/altars

claims that 

| If your god is angry with you when you try to convert an altar, 
| _you_ will be converted to the altar's god instead.


Well, here's the relevant code from pray.c:  

	/* Sacrificing at an altar of a different alignment */
	if (u.ualign.type != altaralign) {
	    /* Is this a conversion ? */
	    /* An unaligned altar in Gehennom will always elicit rejection. */
	    if (ugod_is_angry() || (altaralign == A_NONE && Inhell)) {
            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
		if(u.ualignbase[A_CURRENT] == u.ualignbase[A_ORIGINAL] &&
		 altaralign != A_NONE) {
		  You("have a strong feeling that %s is angry...", u_gname());
		    consume_offering(otmp);
		    pline("%s accepts your allegiance.", a_gname());


On the first glance, it /looks/ like the second spoiler got it right, 
and the first wrong.  However, ugod_is_angry() is not what one could 
guess, but instead 

#define ugod_is_angry() (u.ualign.record < 0)

and u.ualign.record at last is what you would think, namely 
you Alignment score.  So, what really matters is whether 
you have positive alignment or not, and that can easily 
be cured by slaughtering a gazillion foes.  

